'192.168.218.219','192.168.52.37','192.168.156.224','192.168.60.153','192.168.69.116']

You can see here that the ip addresses that are in the remove_list: 192.168.97.225, 192.168.158.170, 192.168.201.40, and 192.168.58.57 are no longer displayed in the ip address list.

# Update the file with the revised list of IP addresses 
After the ip addresses that are in the remove_list were removed, I converted the ip_addresses list back into a string using “ip_addresses = “ ”.join(ip_addresses) and then update the file with another ‘with open(imported_file, “w”) as file:’ so that I can open the file and be able write on it.

Input:
import_file = "allow_list.txt"

remove_list = ["192.168.97.225", "192.168.158.170", "192.168.201.40", "192.168.58.57"]

with open(import_file, "r") as file:
    ip_addresses = file.read()

ip_addresses = ip_addresses.split()

for element in ip_addresses:
    if element in remove_list:
        ip_addresses.remove(element)

ip_addresses = " ".join(ip_addresses)

with open(import_file, "w") as file:
    file.write(ip_addresses)

